  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  With the advent of the spring season, Poseidon set out to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He prepared his armies to defend Atlantis and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of King Poseidon for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Poseidon's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Poseidon was left 
with 3 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Gadeiros
To: Poseidon

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring.  I prepared my forces to defend the Pac. Ocean 
1309 and the surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Gadeiros


